rime-wanxiang (万象拼音) — https://github.com/amzxyz/rime-wanxiang
rime-wanxiang-data — https://github.com/amzxyz/rime-wanxiang-data
RIME-LMDG — https://github.com/amzxyz/RIME-LMDG
Creator: amzxyz
License: CC BY 4.0 (CC-BY-4.0.txt under licenses/)

Resources/Data/rime holds the Wanxiang scheme (standard edition; the release
is named in Licenses/rime-wanxiang-scheme-CC-BY-4.0.txt) with its dictionaries
precompiled by librime. The nine-key schemes, the Weasel settings, the sample
configurations and the README are left out; WoType's settings are written as
*.custom.yaml patches in the user's folder, the scheme files are not changed,
except one line added to lua/wanxiang/auto_phrase.lua: the Memory it creates
disconnects its own notifiers, so deleting a candidate no longer deletes a
second one.
Online dictionary updates come from rime-wanxiang-data and the grammar model
from RIME-LMDG, both downloaded when the user asks for them.

